// src/audit_wire.pdx -- pdxsock M3-002 libpdx-audit integration wire (STUB)
//
// Wave: R100  Milestone: M3-002 (pdxsock#7)
// Doc:  design/networking/r100-user-tools-plan.md §13.6 (paideia-os)
//       + design/tooling/r49-r50-plan.md §3.4         (libpdx-audit contract)
//
// Purpose ---------------------------------------------------------------
// AuditWire is pdxsock's single-file surface for the audit-journal
// integration named at §13.6 of the R100 user-tools plan: every
// completed pdxsock session emits an audit-trail entry (SESSION_START
// at connect / accept, SESSION_CLOSE at pre-shutdown) so a security
// reviewer walking the audit journal can reconstruct network activity
// without needing the semantic-pipe ring.
//
// The two pub-let entry points defined here --
// `pdxsock_audit_session_start` and `pdxsock_audit_session_close` --
// are the callable surface `_start` in main.pdx hooks. Their argument
// ABIs are FROZEN at this landing (peer_ip / peer_port / mode for the
// start half; bytes_in / bytes_out / duration_ns for the close half)
// so a future landing that swaps the STUB body for real libpdx-audit
// calls need touch only THIS file, not main.pdx.
//
// STUB status (M3-002 landing) -----------------------------------------
// The library `paideia-os/libpdx-audit` is not yet in pdxsock's
// `manifest.pdxproj` `deps:` list -- its dispatch table lives in a
// separate satellite ELF whose cross-repo link path is not stitched at
// this milestone. Threading a real dep would additionally require
// `pdxsock`'s `caps.decl` to acquire `KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT(write,
// svc.audit-journal) via svc_lookup` (see libpdx-audit/caps.decl) and
// a `KIND_USER` invoker reference the R100 wave has already listed
// mandatory. Both are follow-up items tracked as `pdxsock.M3-002-b:
// add libpdx-audit dep to manifest + caps.decl + swap AuditWire STUB
// body for real audit_begin / audit_record_output / audit_commit
// calls`.
//
// Until that lands, both entry points execute a no-op body --
// `xor rax, rax; ret` -- and return 0 (matching libpdx-audit's
// `AUDIT_OK = 0` convention). `main.pdx`'s `_start` reads that
// return but treats a 0 as "audit not yet wired; carry on"; a future
// landing where an audit-broker failure MUST kill the run will
// introduce a distinct return-value convention (already matches
// libpdx-audit's `AUDIT_ERR_* != 0` shape).
//
// Effects declaration --------------------------------------------------
// The STUB body touches neither memory nor sysregs, but the DECLARED
// effect set is `!{mem, sysreg} @{cap, sched}` -- the same set the
// real libpdx-audit body will require (`audit_begin` /
// `audit_record_output` / `audit_commit` all declare
// `!{mem, sysreg} @{cap, sched}` per libpdx-audit's audit_client.pdx).
// Declaring the wider set NOW means the swap-to-real landing changes
// only body bytes, not the pub-let signature -- callers in main.pdx
// need no re-typing when the body flips from no-op to real.
//
// `_start` already declares `!{mem, sysreg} @{fs, sched, cap}` so
// this callee's effect / cap set is a strict subset (cap and sched
// both present in the caller) -- the call is well-typed under the
// pdxsock effect algebra.
//
// Event kinds ----------------------------------------------------------
// The wire uses two STUB event codes at this milestone:
//   `PSAW_EVENT_SESSION_START = 200`   (chose 200/201 to sit clear of
//   `PSAW_EVENT_SESSION_CLOSE = 201`    libpdx-audit's own tool-life-
//                                        cycle codes UEJ_KIND_TOOL_
//                                        INVOKE=130, TOOL_OUTPUT=132,
//                                        TOOL_EXIT=133 per libpdx-
//                                        audit/design/architecture.md
//                                        §5.13)
// These are documentation-only at STUB level -- the STUB body does
// not read them. When the swap-to-real landing wires
// `audit_send_record`, they will feed into the `event_kind` arg. If
// libpdx-audit assigns its own canonical `SESSION_*` codes in a
// future revision, this file updates the two constants; call sites
// in main.pdx are unaffected.
//
// Audit-buffer sizing --------------------------------------------------
// `PSAW_AUDIT_RECORD_LEN = 256` documents the byte count the real
// body will marshal into -- libpdx-audit's `PdxAuditRecord@0.2` is a
// 256-byte hybrid record per libpdx-audit#11 + #12 (five u64 numeric
// words at the head, string tail behind them). The STUB body does
// not allocate this buffer; a future landing declares a
// `pdxsock_audit_record_buf : [u8; 256] @align(8)` in main.pdx's
// .bss alongside `pdxsock_record_buf` (the 48-byte
// `SockSessionRecord@0.1` buffer). Two separate buffers -- the
// SockSessionRecord@0.1 body-pipe emit (unchanged from v1.2-B) and
// the audit-journal PdxAuditRecord@0.2 payload -- because they
// travel to distinct consumers (semantic-pipe ring / fd-3 vs. the
// audit journal IPC endpoint) with distinct schemas.
//
// The `SockSessionRecord@0.1` emit at `sys_semantic_send` (SC+ ID
// 115) is NOT DISPLACED by this integration. Both records travel
// on every completed session; the audit-journal path is a security
// review surface, the semantic-pipe path is an observability /
// automation surface, and they carry overlapping but not identical
// data. The bytes-in/out counters live once in `_start`'s r12/r13
// and land in BOTH records via distinct marshal blocks.
//
// Encoder discipline (per user memory `pdx encoder pitfalls`) -----------
//   * no `test rN, rN` (every zero-check is `cmp reg, 0`)
//   * byte loads via `xor rax, rax; mov_b rax, [ptr]` (unused at STUB)
//   * no 2-op `imul r, imm`
//   * no `and reg, imm64` on r8..r15
//   * PascalCase module basename (`AuditWire` from `audit_wire.pdx`)
//   * every label prefixed `psaw_` per the wire-namespace convention
//     the task charter names for this file
//   * SysV push/pop parity: leaf body touches no stack

module AuditWire = structure {

  // -------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Event-kind constants (STUB values; see file header for allocation
  // rationale). Kept as `pub let` u64 constants mirroring the pattern
  // `pdxsock_ssr_magic` / `pdxsock_schema_sock_session` established in
  // main.pdx. Not consumed at STUB level (the STUB body does not load
  // them), but present so:
  //   (a) `grep PSAW_EVENT_SESSION` in the pdxsock tree surfaces the
  //       wire-visible event names at any git-blame moment, and
  //   (b) the swap-to-real landing loads them via `mov r64, imm64`
  //       (movabs) or `mov rax, [rip + PSAW_EVENT_SESSION_START]`
  //       without inventing a symbol.
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------
  pub let PSAW_EVENT_SESSION_START : u64 = 200
  pub let PSAW_EVENT_SESSION_CLOSE : u64 = 201

  // Audit-buffer sizing: documented at file-scope so the swap-to-real
  // landing does not need to invent one. Matches libpdx-audit's
  // `PdxAuditRecord@0.2` fixed 256-byte record.
  pub let PSAW_AUDIT_RECORD_LEN    : u64 = 256

  // -------------------------------------------------------------------
  // pdxsock_audit_session_start(peer_ip, peer_port, mode) -> u64
  //
  //   rdi = peer_ip     (u32-shaped u64; 0 in server mode -- accept
  //                       does not thread a peer-address out-param
  //                       at MVP, per main.pdx `pdxsock_server_body`
  //                       comment)
  //   rsi = peer_port   (u16-shaped u64; 0 in server mode)
  //   rdx = mode        (0 = tcp-client, 1 = tcp-server; matches the
  //                       `r14` mode convention `_start` already uses)
  //   rax = 0 on success (STUB always returns 0)
  //
  // Called from main.pdx immediately after `sys_connect` (client path)
  // or `sys_accept` (server path) returns success. At STUB level,
  // discards every argument and returns 0.
  //
  // Register discipline: pure leaf, no callee-save touched. `rax` is
  // the only write. `rdi`/`rsi`/`rdx` (args) are caller-save --
  // pdxsock's `_start` pushes nothing before the call, so their
  // post-call value is immaterial to the caller.
  //
  // Future real body will:
  //   * marshal a `PdxAuditRecord@0.2` payload from the three args
  //     plus `event_kind = PSAW_EVENT_SESSION_START` and `ts_ns` from
  //     an `rdtsc` snapshot
  //   * call `AuditClient::audit_begin(op_name = "pdxsock",
  //     op_args = <mode-string>)` to allocate an `audit_id`
  //   * call `AuditClient::audit_record_output(audit_id,
  //     schema = PdxAuditRecord@0.2 tag, hash = BLAKE3(payload))`
  //   * return the `audit_id` (nonzero on success) so the pre-close
  //     path can thread it into the SESSION_CLOSE record via
  //     `audit_set_parent`
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------
  pub let pdxsock_audit_session_start : (u64, u64, u64) -> u64
    !{mem, sysreg} @{cap, sched} =
    fn (peer_ip: u64) (peer_port: u64) (mode: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg},
      capabilities: {cap, sched},
      justification: "pdxsock.M3-002 (pdxsock#7) libpdx-audit integration STUB (SESSION_START half). paideia-os/libpdx-audit is not yet in pdxsock's manifest.pdxproj deps at this landing -- see file header on M3-002-b follow-up. STUB body is `xor rax, rax; ret`: sets the AUDIT_OK (0) return, no memory or sysreg touch. Declared effect set !{mem, sysreg} @{cap, sched} intentionally mirrors what the swap-to-real body will require (AuditClient::audit_begin + audit_record_output both declare !{mem, sysreg} @{cap, sched} per libpdx-audit/src/audit_client.pdx) so main.pdx's caller-side call encoding survives the swap without re-typing. Arg ABI frozen: rdi = peer_ip (u32-in-low-32; server = 0), rsi = peer_port (u16-in-low-16; server = 0), rdx = mode (0 = tcp-client, 1 = tcp-server, matches _start's r14 convention). Return value 0 at STUB matches libpdx-audit's AUDIT_OK sentinel; the future real body returns an audit_id (nonzero on success) and a nonzero AUDIT_ERR_* on failure. Register discipline: pure leaf -- writes only rax, touches no callee-save, needs no push/pop, needs no stack. rdi/rsi/rdx (caller-save args) may be freely trashed by any future body. Encoder: `xor rN, rN` for the zero-return (paideia-as encodes as `xor r/m64, r64` REX.W pair, valid on rax); `ret` is the 0xC3 near-return -- SysV stack posture at entry is `[rsp] = return address` (call pushed 8 bytes -> rsp % 16 == 0 at callee), and since this leaf touches no stack it exits with the same posture. No `test`, no 2-op `imul`, no `and reg, imm64` on r8..r15 -- STUB body uses none of them. Label prefix psaw_ per the user memory rule -- no branch labels in this body, so the prefix requirement is trivially satisfied.",
      block: {
        // STUB(libpdx-audit): swap this body for a real
        // `audit_begin` + `audit_record_output` pair once
        // libpdx-audit lands in pdxsock's `deps` and pdxsock's
        // `caps.decl` acquires the audit-journal endpoint grant.
        // Until then, no-op returning AUDIT_OK (0) so the caller's
        // post-call gate treats "audit not wired" as
        // indistinguishable from "audit succeeded".
        xor rax, rax;
        ret;
      }
    }

  // -------------------------------------------------------------------
  // pdxsock_audit_session_close(bytes_in, bytes_out, duration_ns) -> u64
  //
  //   rdi = bytes_in     (u64 accumulator from `_start`'s r12)
  //   rsi = bytes_out    (u64 accumulator from `_start`'s r13)
  //   rdx = duration_ns  (u64 TSC-tick delta from `_start`'s pre-
  //                        marshal `sub rax, [start_ns]`; see main.pdx
  //                        file header on the ns / TSC-tick caveat --
  //                        semantics are cycle counts until user-facing
  //                        `sys_clock_now` lands)
  //   rax = 0 on success (STUB always returns 0)
  //
  // Called from main.pdx at the head of
  // `pdxsock_emit_session_and_exit`, BEFORE the
  // `sys_semantic_send` -> `sys_write(3,...)` -> `sys_shutdown` ->
  // `sys_exit(0)` tail. Discards every argument at STUB level.
  //
  // Future real body will:
  //   * marshal `PdxAuditRecord@0.2` payload from args plus
  //     `event_kind = PSAW_EVENT_SESSION_CLOSE`, `ts_ns` from
  //     `rdtsc`, and (once SESSION_START returned a real
  //     `audit_id`) parent linkage via
  //     `AuditClient::audit_set_parent`
  //   * call `AuditClient::audit_record_output(audit_id, schema,
  //     hash)` followed by `AuditClient::audit_commit(audit_id,
  //     exit_code = 0)` to close the audit
  // -------------------------------------------------------------------
  pub let pdxsock_audit_session_close : (u64, u64, u64) -> u64
    !{mem, sysreg} @{cap, sched} =
    fn (bytes_in: u64) (bytes_out: u64) (duration_ns: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg},
      capabilities: {cap, sched},
      justification: "pdxsock.M3-002 (pdxsock#7) libpdx-audit integration STUB (SESSION_CLOSE half). Symmetric peer of pdxsock_audit_session_start -- same STUB shape (xor rax, rax; ret), same declared effect/cap set (!{mem, sysreg} @{cap, sched}, mirroring the future audit_record_output + audit_commit tail per libpdx-audit/src/audit_client.pdx), same STUB return value 0 (AUDIT_OK). Arg ABI frozen: rdi = bytes_in (u64, from _start's r12 accumulator over sys_recv returns), rsi = bytes_out (u64, from _start's r13 accumulator over sys_send returns), rdx = duration_ns (u64, computed at emit_session_and_exit as `session_end_ns - session_start_ns` in TSC ticks -- semantics stable across the ticks->ns rename that sys_clock_now will eventually enable). Register discipline: pure leaf, writes only rax, touches no callee-save, needs no push/pop, needs no stack. Encoder discipline identical to pdxsock_audit_session_start (no test, no 2-op imul, no wide-and on r8..r15, no branch labels so psaw_ prefix requirement is trivially satisfied). Future real body will also load PSAW_EVENT_SESSION_CLOSE via `mov rax, [rip + PSAW_EVENT_SESSION_CLOSE]` (rip-relative u64 load, proven at sys_semantic_send.pdx line 214) before threading it into audit_send_record.",
      block: {
        // STUB(libpdx-audit): swap this body for a real
        // `audit_record_output` + `audit_commit` pair once
        // libpdx-audit lands in pdxsock's `deps`. Until then,
        // no-op returning AUDIT_OK (0) so the caller's post-call
        // gate treats "audit not wired" as indistinguishable from
        // "audit succeeded".
        xor rax, rax;
        ret;
      }
    }

}
